{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01RcAqEyxHar11i22pUaNPf9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# CONFIGS.md -- the configuration surface of the C library\n2\t\n3\tMirror image of `ERRORS.md`: every *valid* configuration the C code branches on.\n4\tDerived from the source, not from guesswork -- the axes below are exactly the\n5\t`#if`/`#ifdef`s of the build, the `if`/`switch` branches the exported functions\n6\ttake on their arguments, and the input shapes those branches distinguish.\n7\t\n8\tEach row is checked by calling **both** shared objects through `dlsym` with many\n9\trandomized inputs (fixed seed per test, `tests/harness/mod.rs::Rng`) plus the\n10\thand-picked boundary values of that row, and comparing every output byte\n11\t(`f32::to_bits()`) and every returned integer.\n12\t\n13\t## Axis 0 -- build configuration (compile time)\n14\t\n15\t`c_src/CMakeLists.txt` has no options: it always compiles `src/q_math.c` and\n16\t`src/main.c` with `-Iinc -Isrc` and links `m`.  The preprocessor axes inside the\n17\tsources are therefore all pinned, and there is exactly **one** build\n18\tconfiguration:\n19\t\n20\t| C axis | where | value in this build | consequence |\n21\t|---|---|---|---|\n22\t| `idppc` | q_shared.h:70, q_math.c:490 | `0` | `#if !idppc` is taken -> `Q_rsqrt` and `Q_fabs` are compiled (the only alternative would be a PowerPC intrinsic version) |\n23\t| `id386` / `idppc_altivec` | q_shared.h:69,71 | `0` | no asm paths |\n24\t| `Q3_VM` | q_shared.h:50 | undefined | system headers, not `bg_lib.h`; the commented-out `assert`s stay out |\n25\t| `__linux__` | q_shared.h:85 | defined | `ID_INLINE` = `inline`, `PATH_SEP='/'`, `BigShort/BigLong/BigFloat` inline decls (never defined -> unused) |\n26\t| `#if 1` | q_shared.h:363 | taken | `DotProduct`, `VectorSubtract`, `VectorAdd`, `VectorCopy`, `VectorScale`, `VectorMA` are the **macro** forms; the `_`-prefixed functions are compiled but never called internally |\n27\t