nap_vector_overflow      (ERRORS.md row 27: the (int) cast of an out-of-range or\n                             NaN component - gcc emits cvttss2si which yields\n                             0x80000000, so the component becomes -2147483648.0f.\n                             Assert C and Rust agree AND that the value really is\n                             -2147483648.0f for those inputs.)\n  macro_forms               (row 55: w_DotProduct/w_VectorSubtract/w_VectorAdd/\n                             w_VectorCopy/w_VectorScale/w_VectorMA/w_VectorClear/\n                             w_VectorSet/w_Vector4Copy/w_MAKERGB/w_MAKERGBA;\n                             20000 random inputs each. ALSO cross-check the macro\n                             forms against the `_`-prefixed function forms from\n                             libcdriver.so (_DotProduct, _VectorAdd,\n                             _VectorSubtract, _VectorCopy, _VectorScale,\n                             _VectorMA) on identical inputs - q_shared.h's `#if 1`\n                             makes the macros the ones actually used, and both\n                             must agree bit-for-bit.)\n  sqrtfast_isnan_square     (row 56: w_SQRTFAST, w_IS_NAN, w_Square. For w_IS_NAN\n                             sweep every exponent/mantissa class incl. +-inf\n                             (which the macro also reports as \"NaN\") and all NaN\n                             payloads.)\n  deg_rad_and_short_angles  (row 57: w_DEG2RAD, w_RAD2DEG (both return double!),\n                             w_ANGLE2SHORT (int), w_SHORT2ANGLE (double),\n                             w_ColorIndex (int, sweep all 256 char values and\n                             negative ints))\n  angle2short_overflow      (ERRORS.md row 26: w_ANGLE2SHORT with values whose\n                             (int) conversion overflows (|x*65536/360| >= 2^31),\n                             plus NaN and ±inf -> 0x80000000 & 65535 == 0)\n  plane_type_for_normal     (row 58: w_PlaneTypeForNormal - normals {1,y,z},\n                             {x,1,z}, {x,y,1}, none == 1.0 (PLANE_NON_AXIAL),\n                             0.99999994 vs 1.0, -1.0, NaN, random)\n  layout_and_constants      (row 60: w_layout(int out[9]) and\n                             w_angle_indexes(int out[10]) and w_M_PI() -> double.\n                             Read tests/csupport/wrappers.c for what each slot\n                             holds, compare all slots, and additionally assert the\n                             concrete expected values: sizeof(cplane_t)==20,\n                             offsets 0,12,16,17,18, NUMVERTEXNORMALS==162,\n                             nanmask==255<<23, sizeof(vec_t)==4, PITCH/YAW/ROLL\n                             ==0/1/2, PLANE_X..PLANE_NON_AXIAL==0..3,\n                             qfalse/qtrue==0/1, sizeof(qboolean)==4, and that\n                             w_M_PI() is exactly std::f64::consts::PI.)\n\n=== FILE 2: tests/data.rs ===\n  data_symbols_match        (row 59: for each exported data symbol, take the\n                             address from BOTH shared objects with\n                             cdata::<T>(name) / rdata::<T>(name) and compare the\n                             raw bytes (u32 bit patterns), element by element:\n                             vec3_origin [f32;3], axisDefault [[f32;3];3],\n                             bytedirs [[f32;3];162], g_color_table [[f32;4];8],\n                             and the eleven vec4_t colours colorBlack, colorRed,\n                             colorGreen, colorBlue, colorYellow, colorMagenta,\n                             colorCyan, colorWhite, colorLtGrey, colorMdGrey,\n                             colorDkGrey. Report the index of any mismatch.)\n  data_symbols_are_writable (the C symbols live in .data/.bss and are NOT const;\n                             write a value through the pointer, read it back,\n                             restore it - do this for both .so's vec3_origin and\n                             assert both behave the same. Restore the original\n                             values afterwards so other tests are unaffected.)\n  bytedirs_used_by_bytetodir (cross-check: for b in 0..162, ByteToDir(b, out) must\n                             return exactly bytedirs[b] as read from the SAME .so,\n                             for both C and Rust.)\n\nWORKFLOW: write both files, then run\n  cd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-MbXgVZ/translated_rust\n  ./build_c.sh >/dev/null && cargo build --offline 2>&1 | tail -3\n  timeout 600 cargo test --offline --test qshared 2>&1 | tail -40\n  timeout 600 cargo test --offline --test data 2>&1 | tail -40\nIterate until both compile. Report the final test summaries, the list of test fns\nper file, and any divergence (exact inputs + bit patterns) WITHOUT fixing src/.","uuid":"80cb1d17-991c-4f9c-8920-a2e616307ee2","session_id":"bf9d36cb-13a4-40a8-a93d-48ad7b006df9"}
