ts` triples + a 53x53 pattern cross product), `ClearBounds` and `AddPointToBounds`, where no arithmetic can make a payload compiler-dependent.\n- Aliasing: `out==arg1`, `out==arg2`, `arg1==arg2`, and all-same-pointer for add/sub/MA; `out==in` for scale/copy/Vector4Scale/normalize2/NormalizeColor/VectorRotate; `out==in1`, `out==in2`, `in1==in2`, all-three for MatrixMultiply; `mins==maxs` for ClearBounds/AddPointToBounds/RadiusFromBounds. `clear_bounds` additionally covers partially overlapping buffers (`maxs = mins+1..3`), which the right-to-left chained assignment makes well defined.\n- Row-specific coverage: `_DotProduct` gets all 55x55 shape pairs + SEQ (same pointer twice) + 20000 random pairs; `VectorNormalize`/`VectorNormalize2` cover all three length classes including `{1e-30,0,0}` and `{1.084202_2e-19,0,0}` / `{1.084202_3e-19,0,0}` straddling the underflow edge, plus NaN/inf lengths, and check both the returned length and the (possibly unmodified) vector.\n\n## Divergences found\n\n**None.** C and Rust agree bit-for-bit on every case, including the `0*inf` NaN manufacture in `_VectorMA`, `inf-inf` in `_VectorSubtract`, signed-zero results, `f32::MAX+f32::MAX` overflow, the `length==0` underflow branch of `VectorNormalize` (vector left unmodified) vs `VectorNormalize2` (`out` cleared), and all aliased/overlapping pointer modes.\n\n## Verification that the tests are not vacuous\n\nI temporarily injected two negative controls into `tests/vectors.rs`, confirmed both failed, then restored the file byte-for-byte (verified with `diff`):\n- XOR-ing bit 0 of the Rust `_DotProduct` result → `dot_product` failed with `C returned -1.4717771e26 (0xeaf37c2f) but Rust returned -1.471777e26 (0xeaf37c2e)`.\n- Perturbing the guard slot of the Rust `ClearBounds` buffer → `clear_bounds` failed.\n\n## One pre-existing issue worth flagging (not mine, not fixed)\n\n`cargo build --tests` / plain `cargo test` fails on the **lib test target** with:\n```\nerror: entry symbol `main` dec