\n1. **Row 42 — an inverted box can never `return 3`.** `if (p->dist <= emins[type]) return 1;` is tested first, so with `emins[t]=10, emaxs[t]=0, dist=5` the C returns **1**, not 3. `3` is reachable only for a properly ordered box with `emins[t] < dist < emaxs[t]`.\n\n2. **ERRORS.md row 22 — a NaN in `emins`/`emaxs` alone does *not* give 0.** Each `switch` arm builds `dist1` from one corner and `dist2` from the other, so a NaN in a single slot of only one corner poisons only one of the two sums and the surviving comparison still fires. Exact case: `emins={NaN,-1,-1}, emaxs={1,1,1}, normal={1,1,1}, dist=0.0, type=3, signbits=0` → `dist1 = 3.0` (from `emaxs`), `dist2 = NaN` → returns **1**. Returning 0 requires both sums poisoned: NaN in `p->dist`, in `p->normal[i]`, or in the *same* slot of both corners. The test now asserts 0 for those shapes and asserts `!= 3` for the single-corner shapes.\n\n3. **Row 40 — a degenerate triangle can return `qtrue` when products overflow.** For `b == c` the cross product computes `d[i]*d[j] - d[j]*d[i]`, which is exactly `0` in IEEE *unless* the product overflows: then `inf - inf = NaN`, `VectorNormalize` returns NaN, and `if (length)` is true for NaN. Exact case `a={0,0,0}, b=c={1e20,-1e20,7}`: `plane = {0x7fc00000, 0x7fc00000, 0x7fc00000}` (i.e. all NaN), `plane[3] = NaN`, **return 1** — and `plane[3]` *is* written. Both libraries agree. The guaranteed-`qfalse` point set is now capped below the overflow threshold (~1.8e19); a separate `wild` set covers the overflowing shapes with C-vs-Rust-only assertions.\n\n## Coverage notes\n\n- All output buffers pre-filled with distinct finite sentinels (`0x7DEADBE0..4`), with a guard slot past the end; `plane_from_points` asserts `plane[3] untouched == (return == qfalse)` on every single call.\n- `SetPlaneSignbits` and `BoxOnPlaneSide` compare the **whole 20-byte** `cplane_t` (via `copy_nonoverlapping` into `[u8;20]`), and additionally assert C leaves `normal`/`dist`/`type`/`pad` (and both box arrays) unmodified. `size_of`/`align_of` are const-asserted at 20/4.\n- Row 43 asserts all four of `0,1,2,3` occur **for each of the 8 signbits arms** (crafted via `normal={1,0,0}`, which collapses the arm to `dist1=A, dist2=B`).\n- Row 44b asserts the exact `default:`-arm truth table (`dist<0`→1, `-0.0`/`0.0`→1, `>0`→2, `NaN`→0) over signbits 8..255 × type {3,4,128,255}, and that `3` is *unreachable* there.\n- Row 44a cross-checks every `type` in 3..=255 against a `type=3` reference for the identical box/plane.\n- `DirToByte`: verified all 162 `bytedirs` entries map to their own index (also independently pre-verified in float32 arithmetic before asserting), plus negations, scalings, zero (→0), `NULL` (→0), extremes, and 25 000 random.\n\nUnrelated pre-existing issue: `cargo build --tests` / `cargo test --lib` fails with `entry symbol main declared multiple times` on the **lib unit-test** target (cdylib + `#[no_mangle] main`). It predates my change and does not affect integration-test targets — use `cargo test --test <name>`. Also note other agents were concurrently adding `tests/{angles,errors,vectors,driver_cli}.rs` and touched `src/q_shared.rs`; my test passes against the current state of the tree."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":516,"cache_read_input_tokens":123662,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":516,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01PqgGZDVkADyukTKaEnPx7K","session_id":"bf9d36cb-13a4-40a8-a93d-48ad7b006df9","uuid":"a7984efd-3ed0-4cab-b7db-cc5e1ef3fc98","timestamp":"2026-08-20T13:55:51.959Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write plane/dir differential tests"}
