{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_f6wpmk3dlgvuji6jsgh7x63cljq6z6ihxbeyfffpf7ux43c4q6ha","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Summary\n\nThe prior translation covered only 3 things reachable from `main()` (`VectorNormalizeFast`, `Q_rsqrt`, `DotProduct`) out of a 1012-line C file. **The whole library is now translated and differentially verified.**\n\n### Phase A — artifacts\n| file | content |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | all 63 symbols of the C `.so` (47 functions incl. `main` + 15 data objects) — **0 missing** from the Rust cdylib, 0 undefined non-libc imports |\n| `ERRORS.md` | 50 rows, one per distinct rejection/edge in the C (grepped from every early `return`, guard, `switch default:`, clamp, loop bound, cast overflow) |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | 67 valid-path rows over the real axes: `cplane_t.type`/`signbits` modes, `AngleVectors`' 8 NULL combinations, 10 input shapes, pointer aliasing, and all 6 call-hierarchy levels |\n| `NOTES.md` | every faithfulness decision + the 4 documented deviations |\n\nTranslated: all of `q_math.c`, all executable parts of `q_shared.h` (25 macros + 8 `static ID_INLINE` functions, exposed for testing via 36 `w_*` hooks on both sides), and `main.c` as the exported `main` symbol that the `#![no_main]` binary reuses.\n\n### Phases B–D — 101 tests, 9 binaries, 4 configurations, all passing\nEverything is called through `dlsym` on `cbuild/libcdriver.so`, `cbuild/libcwrap.so` and `target/*/libdriver.so`; results compared via `to_bits()`.\n\n**Three real bugs found and fixed in the Rust:**\n1. `RAD2DEG` — `180.0f` is a *float* literal, so C rounds `a*180.0f` to `f32` before dividing by `M_PI`; the translation multiplied in `f64` (wrong for ~98% of inputs, and `1e38` gave `5.7e39` instead of `inf`).\n2. `ColorIndex` — `c - '0'` overflows for `c < INT_MIN+48`; gcc wraps, debug Rust panicked → `wrapping_sub`.\n3. `AngleVectors` — gcc folds `-1*sr` into an `xorps` sign flip, which flips a NaN's sign where `mulss` by `-1.0f` does not; now bit-exact over all 5 832 NaN/inf angle combinations.\n\n**Hazards found in the C and documented:** `AngleVectors` is not reentrant (`static float sr,sp,...` — the C corrupts itself under libtest's threads); `ColorBytes3` never writes byte 3; `AngleSubtract` and `Q_log2(negative)` never terminate; `PlaneFromPoints` returns `qtrue` for a degenerate triangle when the cross product overflows.\n\n**Honesty checks:** `./mutation_check.sh` injects 12 mutations — all 12 are caught. `DIFF_STRICT_NAN=1` turns off the single documented tolerance (NaN *payload* selection when two different NaNs meet in one expression — gcc -O0 picks the `mulss` source operand per call site) and prints the exact 12-test residual, tabulated in `NOTES.md`. The harness also fails loudly if a `.so` is older than its sources, since `cargo test` does not rebuild the cdylib."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":757,"cache_read_input_tokens":441365,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":757,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bf9d36cb-13a4-40a8-a93d-48ad7b006df9","uuid":"6ae28fe6-b7d4-4bd2-a469-dd7d4dbb1158","timestamp":"2026-08-20T14:22:16.574Z"}
